<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ming Sheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1356">1356</a>–1393</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ming Sheng was the second and last ruler of Ming Xia, a state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> founded by his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-yuzhen">Ming Yuzhen</a> during the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>. He succeeded as a child in 1366 under regents. In 1371 armies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> invaded and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chongqing">Chongqing</a> surrendered; he was given a noble title and later sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, where he died.</p></div>
